WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.430
Netflix has enjoyed a bunch of well-deserved
success with their original content.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.290
No commercials and fewer content restrictions
have given the the streaming service a clear

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:12.160
edge over other networks — and they don't
seem to be slowing down any time soon.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.440
But with expanded original programming, not
everything can survive.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.360
Since Netflix doesn't disclose their ratings,
the reason for a show's demise is sometimes

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.360
a mystery.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.110
Here's a look at the real reason why Netflix
gave up on these shows.

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:25.250
Lilyhammer

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:30.190
Netflix's first outing into original programming
was Lilyhammer, about a mob fixer who enters

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:33.460
the Witness Protection Program after a failed
attempt on his life.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:37.760
Co-writer and star Steven Van Zandt wasn't
too pleased about the show's cancellation,

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.510
writing on Twitter: "#Lilyhammer RIP.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:41.510
Not my decision.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:43.739
Let's just say for now the business got too
complicated."

00:00:43.739 --> 00:00:47.710
Lilyhammer was produced in a partnership between
Netflix and the Norwegian government-owned

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:50.190
broadcasting company NRK.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.899
Netflix chief content officer Ted Sarandos
cited the partnership as the source of the

00:00:53.899 --> 00:00:57.079
decision to give Lilyhammer the axe, telling
The Hollywood Reporter,

00:00:57.079 --> 00:01:00.701
"It was very difficult to maintain the level
of global exclusivity and control that we

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:03.890
hope to with our shows with [Lilyhammer] and
the way it was structured with the Norwegian

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.890
broadcaster."

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.400
Gypsy

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.680
Starring Naomi Watts as a therapist who oversteps
all boundaries with her patients, Gypsy was

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.240
cancelled only six weeks after its release.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.840
Reviews were not kind, though many applauded
Watts and co-star Billy Crudup for their work,

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.270
given the subpar material.

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:21.970
The Telegraph described the show as…

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:23.040
"...flavourless hodgepodge."

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.620
And The AV Club said it was...

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:25.990
"...as subtle as syphilis."

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:29.430
Along with the critical bombing were reports
of an inflated salary for Watts.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:33.970
Add to that the objections raised by Roma
organizations in regards to the series' title,

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:36.780
and it seems Gypsy was doomed from the start.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.470
Haters Back Off

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:42.640
Netflix experimented with transporting a YouTube
character into a more traditional scripted

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.840
series with Haters Back Off, but apparently,
it didn't quite work as planned.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:51.040
The show follows the inexplicable rise of
the talentless character Miranda Sings.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.100
The reason for its cancellation doesn't seem
to be too much of a mystery.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:58.140
Overall, the consensus seemed to be that the
transition from short YouTube clips of Miranda

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:00.770
Sings to half hour episodes wasn't easy.

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:05.010
According to the Los Angeles Daily News, while
Miranda's utter lack of talent might be hilarious

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:10.090
as a short video online, that simply doesn't
sustain a 30-minute show.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:11.459
The Get Down

00:02:11.459 --> 00:02:15.879
Baz Luhrmann's ambitious musical drama The
Get Down was canceled after one season — and

00:02:15.879 --> 00:02:17.599
enough problems to fill a concert hall.

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:21.900
Variety reported that production delays became
so frequent that the writers started jokingly

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.829
calling the show "The Shut Down."

00:02:23.829 --> 00:02:28.659
With a budget of $120 million, The Get Down
was reportedly the most expensive production

00:02:28.659 --> 00:02:32.269
in Netflix history, which likely would have
been a huge factor in the decision to cut

00:02:32.269 --> 00:02:33.269
the show.

00:02:33.269 --> 00:02:36.659
But Luhrmann has said he believes the cancellation
had less to do with money and more to do with

00:02:36.659 --> 00:02:39.190
his decision to walk away from the project
to work on a movie.

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:43.299
He addressed his fans on Facebook, saying:
"It kills me that I can’t split myself into

00:02:43.299 --> 00:02:45.340
two and make myself available to both productions.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.239
… But the simple truth is, I make movies."

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:49.299
Lady Dynamite

00:02:49.299 --> 00:02:54.650
The unique and intense stand-up comic Maria
Bamford played herself in Netflix's Lady Dynamite.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.780
Critics and viewers alike were thrilled with
this surreal comedy full of sharp critique

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:01.050
on Hollywood as well as painful humor about
mental illness.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:04.659
Following the show's cancellation announcement,
some of Bamford's comments suggest she simply

00:03:04.659 --> 00:03:06.870
couldn't continue with the production schedule.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:10.990
Speaking to the AV Club, she described the
difficulty of working 15-hour days and the

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.870
irony of her work on the show, saying,

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:16.599
"It's hilarious because [Lady Dynamite] is
about mental health and that [I was] kind

00:03:16.599 --> 00:03:20.810
of putting my mental health in danger in order
to do a TV show about mental health.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.220
So, whoops."

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:23.220
Bloodline

00:03:23.809 --> 00:03:27.720
The cancellation of Bloodline — a dramatic
thriller about a family reeling at the skeletons

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:32.059
uncovered in its closets — came as a surprise,
particularly considering the first season's

00:03:32.059 --> 00:03:34.109
appeal to both critics and viewers.

00:03:34.109 --> 00:03:37.639
Reception for the second season wasn't nearly
as positive as it was for the first, though

00:03:37.639 --> 00:03:41.309
it seems likely the biggest factor in the
show's cancellation was the end of Florida's

00:03:41.309 --> 00:03:43.540
entertainment tax incentive program.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:47.010
Bloodline's budget benefited from what could've
been a much more expensive venture.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:50.999
Once that changed — on top of a less positive
critical response — Bloodline's fate was

00:03:50.999 --> 00:03:52.319
sealed.

00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:53.650
Sense8

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:57.930
The cancellation of Sense8 after two seasons
was perhaps the most surprising of Netflix's

00:03:57.930 --> 00:03:59.010
cuts to date.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:03.129
Filmed in various cities across the globe,
the show was a hit with both fans and critics.

00:04:03.129 --> 00:04:07.079
According to the Hollywood Reporter, Netflix
chief content officer Ted Sarandos said,

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:10.859
"The audience was very passionate, but not
large enough to support the economics of something

00:04:10.859 --> 00:04:12.729
that big, even on our platform."

00:04:12.729 --> 00:04:18.079
At a cost of $9 million per episode, Sense8
was simply too expensive to keep making.

00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:22.180
Fan outcry was strong enough to merit an apologetic
response from Netflix on Facebook, saying:

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:25.830
"The reason we've taken so long to get back
to you is because we've thought long and hard

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:29.590
here at Netflix to try to make it work but
unfortunately we can't."

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:33.630
But later in the month, Netflix changed its
mind, greenlighting a special two-hour series

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:36.610
finale for Sense8 set for release in 2018.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:37.610
Thanks for watching!

